WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.712
A raw file is flexible, but Spark may need to infer or be given the schema.

00:00:05.712 --> 00:00:09.807
A curated Delta table has a stronger table contract.

00:00:09.807 --> 00:00:17.192
For teaching, think of raw files as ingestion material and tables as reusable analytical assets.

00:00:17.192 --> 00:00:21.382
That is not an absolute rule, but it is a helpful workflow.

00:00:21.382 --> 00:00:26.582
A lakehouse combines scalable file-based storage with table-management features.

00:00:26.582 --> 00:00:35.192
Delta-style tables add transaction logs, schema controls, and reliable table operations on top of object

00:00:35.192 --> 00:00:35.592
storage.

00:00:35.592 --> 00:00:41.412
Keep raw ingestion, cleaned data, and curated analytical tables conceptually separate so lineage remains

00:00:41.412 --> 00:00:43.087
clear.
